I published https://www.npmjs.com/package/electron-extension-installer as a temporary workaround for some common extensions, including React, but this really should be fixed on electrons end. (source code [here](https://github.com/reporter/electron-extension-installer))


```typescript
import { installExtension, REACT_DEVELOPER_TOOLS } from "electron-extension-installer";

app.on("ready", async () => {
  await installExtension(REACT_DEVELOPER_TOOLS, {
    loadExtensionOptions: {
      allowFileAccess: true,
    },
  });
});
```

Hi, has anyone had any luck in using the [Angular DevTools extension](https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/angular-devtools/ienfalfjdbdpebioblfackkekamfmbnh)? I'm testing version 1.0.37 with Electron 36.3.1, I'm able to load the extension, but when clicking on the Angular tab in the Chrome DevTools, it says "Angular application not detected" (see pic below).

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a128007-9646-4609-878c-9ea16b707374)

this is how i'm loading the extension:

```
const angularDevToolsPath = path.join(__dirname, '../../../../../..', 'AngularDevTools', '1.0.37_0');
console.log('angularDevToolsPath', angularDevToolsPath);
if (fs.existsSync(angularDevToolsPath)) {
  console.log('LOADING ANGULAR DEVTOOLS', angularDevToolsPath);
  const extension = await session.defaultSession.extensions.loadExtension(angularDevToolsPath);
  console.log('Angular DevTools extension loaded:', extension.name, extension.id, extension.version);
}
```

